cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this was useful in your work, please cite it."
title: "Reproducing a published IFEval score on one shared GPU: three arms, a pre-registration chain, and a paired test"
abstract: "A first-hand reproduction of the IFEval score published for Agents-A1-4B on a single RTX 4090. Prompt-level strict accuracy is 76.9 over all 541 prompts under a fully stated deterministic setting, against a model-card value of 94.8 whose metric variant, decoding and thinking budget are unstated. A thinking-mode arm scored 87.5 on a cost-capped subsample of 32 prompts, which looks like an eleven-point gain until the pre-registered paired test shows the first arm scores 87.5 on those same prompts. Also reported: the official scorer is not deterministic, and batched bf16 decoding is not bit-exact across batch compositions."
type: software
